// A body with no declaration to attach to. `@target(.X)` is ALWAYS a body
// (plan decision 5), so it needs exactly one `@target` declaration of the same
// name and signature in the module. There is none here — the sibling declares
// `platform_name`, not `platform_tag`.
//
// This is R2036, and it is the mistake users will make most often: a typo in
// the name silently produces "a body for nothing" rather than an override.

module "main"

@target
export platform_name :: fn() -> string = "posix"

main :: fn() -> void {}
